{"schema": 1, "kind": "review", "id": "rev-20261112T060546Z-9c66cc62", "ts": "2026-11-12T06:13:08Z", "actor": {"worktree": "integ-pool", "plugin": "3.8.1-dev", "branch": "chore/integration-on-the-pool"}, "body": {"base_commit": "fc27e5d40330e57204d118217eee497a1d0260f5", "base_tree": "9253c95fac73a2ca3c0ea330e2be0b2f6f88a8a3", "head_tree": "60a214613d1315a8ee044f55a4d47e652a68961b", "head_commit": null, "dispatch_commit": "fc27e5d40330e57204d118217eee497a1d0260f5", "mode": "chunk (lighter pass, not ready for push)", "mode_chosen_by": "explicit-args", "stage": "inner", "tier": "standard", "roster": [{"role": "reviewer", "model": "claude-opus-5-5"}], "files_reviewed": [".testament.toml", "conftest.py", "docs/testing.md", "packages/core/src/threetears/core/testing/fixtures.py", "packages/core/src/threetears/core/testing/services.py", "packages/core/tests/integration/test_process_services.py", "packages/core/tests/unit/testing/test_container_stagger.py", "pyproject.toml", "scripts/test-integration.sh", "scripts/test.sh", "tests/enforcement/test_integration_suite_selection.py", "tests/enforcement/test_require_services_backstop.py", "tests/enforcement/test_secrets_marker.py", "tests/require_services.py", "tests/test_test_integration_script.py", "tests/test_test_sh_script.py", "uv.lock"], "files_changed": [".testament.toml", "conftest.py", "docs/testing.md", "packages/core/src/threetears/core/testing/fixtures.py", "packages/core/src/threetears/core/testing/services.py", "packages/core/tests/integration/test_process_services.py", "packages/core/tests/unit/testing/test_container_stagger.py", "pyproject.toml", "scripts/test-integration.sh", "scripts/test.sh", "tests/enforcement/test_integration_suite_selection.py", "tests/enforcement/test_require_services_backstop.py", "tests/enforcement/test_secrets_marker.py", "tests/require_services.py", "tests/test_test_integration_script.py", "tests/test_test_sh_script.py", "uv.lock"], "files_oracle": [], "findings": [{"goal": "Nothing Is Broken", "severity": "blocking", "title": "test-integration.sh's pool part fails exit 2, and points back to test-integration.sh, whenever an env gate (RECORD, THREETEARS_LIVE_*, TAVILY_API_KEY) is set. The path has no test.", "recommendation": "instance. scripts/test-integration.sh:160-178 picks the pool route from testament on PATH, CI and TESTAMENT alone. It then calls `./scripts/test.sh --suite integration <paths>`. test.sh:150-153 sets local_only for any env gate, which skips the pool branch (test.sh:239) and reaches the refusal at test.sh:266-269 ('--suite integration selects a suite on the testament pool, and this run is local; the integration suite's local form is scripts/test-integration.sh'). Scenario: a developer with TAVILY_API_KEY (newly a gate in this change), RECORD or a THREETEARS_LIVE_* variable exported runs `./scripts/test-integration.sh -rs`. scheduled-jobs and the process-services file run nowhere, the run exits 2, and the message sends the developer back to the script they just ran. Fix: decide the behaviour and pin it with a test in tests/test_test_integration_script.py. Either test-integration.sh clears test.sh's gates for the pool call (the integration suite already deselects `secrets`), or it refuses up front and names the gate. Do not send the moved packages local; that would load the laptop.", "files": ["scripts/test-integration.sh", "scripts/test.sh", "tests/test_test_integration_script.py"], "fid": "R-1"}], "counts": {"blocking": 1, "warning": 0, "note": 0}, "observations": [{"goal": "Nothing Is Unintended", "title": "CI's integration job now collects test_process_services.py and skips all 13 of its tests, and so does any run off the pool", "recommendation": "ACCEPT is the default. The module's autouse session fixture (test_process_services.py:51-55) skips everywhere outside process mode. CI's `pytest packages/core ... -m integration -v` and the no-testament or TESTAMENT=off route of test-integration.sh (which moves POOL to LOCAL with no --ignore) each gain 13 permanent skips. docs/testing.md's 'Legitimate skips on a dev box' list does not name them, and CLAUDE.md says to account for every skip. A cheap fix, batched into the next commit: skip collecting the file outside process mode (a `collect_ignore` / `pytest_ignore_collect` in packages/core/tests/integration/conftest.py keyed on THREETEARS_TEST_SERVICES). The pool sets the variable, so the pool still collects the file. Otherwise list the 13 as a legitimate skip in docs/testing.md.", "files": ["packages/core/tests/integration/test_process_services.py", "docs/testing.md"], "oid": "O-1"}, {"goal": "Nothing Is Broken", "title": "moto readiness accepts ANY server answering on the picked port, so a port race can wire one batch to another batch's moto", "recommendation": "instance. services.py:897-913 with _s3_answers (822-859). Process A and process B pick the same free port. B's moto binds first and A's moto then dies with 'Address already in use'. A's HTTP probe has already reached B's server, or reaches it before A's `stopped()` is polled, so it returns True. A creates its bucket on B's server and runs its tests there, and loses the server when B tears down. Postgres reads its own log and NATS uses -p -1, so neither has this race. Fix: accept readiness only while `child.poll() is None` both before and after the answering probe. Better, have moto bind port 0 and report the port.", "files": ["packages/core/src/threetears/core/testing/services.py"], "oid": "O-2"}, {"goal": "Nothing Is Broken", "title": "the selection enforcement lets a docker or secrets file sit under a suite path, as long as it is also under a LOCAL_DIRS path. That file then runs nowhere", "recommendation": "test_docker_and_secrets_tests_run_here (test_integration_suite_selection.py:106-117) requires only that the file lie under a LOCAL_DIRS path ('whatever else holds it'). test-integration.sh:184-193 then adds `--ignore` for every suite path inside a local directory, and the pool deselects docker and secrets. So a docker-marked file listed individually in the suite (the shape test_process_services.py has inside core's local dir) is deselected on the pool and ignored here. No instance exists today. Add the converse assertion, that no docker or secrets file lies under any suite path. That makes the stricter rule sound until C7.", "files": ["tests/enforcement/test_integration_suite_selection.py"], "oid": "O-3"}, {"goal": "Nothing Is Broken", "title": "the changed stagger test is not weakened, but its new `\"running_\" in source` assertion is vacuous", "recommendation": "Verdict on the CHANGED test: the contract holds and is wider. Every function in fixtures and services that calls PostgresContainer, DockerContainer or nats_server must call stagger_container_start. That covers the three moved container routes and searxng, and the control (at least 4) makes an empty walk fail. The old check was a substring test on four fixtures; this one also catches any new starter. One part is vacuous: test_container_stagger.py:107-109 checks `\"running_\" in inspect.getsource(...)`, and db_container, nats_container and s3_container each name running_postgres, running_nats or running_s3 in their docstrings. The assertion therefore cannot fail. Make it an AST check for a Call to `running_*`, like the walk below it. A related point: test_an_external_database_skips_the_container_and_the_wait still monkeypatches `fixtures.stagger_container_start`. db and NATS now stagger through `services.stagger_container_start`, so for those two the guard is only as strong as it was on a Docker-less host, where it was already weak. Patch both modules.", "files": ["packages/core/tests/unit/testing/test_container_stagger.py"], "oid": "O-4"}, {"goal": "Nothing Is Missing", "title": "docs say test-integration.sh needs Docker and runs containers, and do not mention its pool route", "recommendation": "docs/testing.md:302-307 ('they spin real NATS and Postgres containers and need Docker'), README.md:156 ('against real containers ... (needs Docker)') and docs/testing.md:127 ('Run ./scripts/test-integration.sh -rs as always', under 'When the pool is down') are now partly false. scheduled-jobs and the process-services file run on the pool, and with the pool down that part exits 2 unless TESTAMENT=off is given with a reason. CLAUDE.md:155 lists the env gates without TAVILY_API_KEY. Prose: delete the claims, or make them relational ('test-integration.sh runs the suite's paths on the pool and LOCAL_DIRS here; see the script'), now rather than in C7.", "files": ["docs/testing.md"], "oid": "O-5"}, {"goal": "Nothing Is Broken", "title": "the process-mode lifecycle has small holes: sweep robustness, the shared-root trust, a partial owner-file read, atexit after fork, and a failed initdb", "recommendation": "Verified sound: the pid plus start-time check (stat field 22, zombies counted as gone) never kills a live owner's server or a reused pid. Every server stops on test failure, KeyboardInterrupt and pytest.fail, through finally blocks and fixture teardown, and SIGKILL or a batch timeout is left to the next sweep. initdb is per process, so concurrent processes share no template. The holes: (1) services.py:331 `mkdir(exist_ok=True)` accepts a /tmp/threetears-svc owned by another uid, or a symlink. The sweep trusts the `pids` files under it, so a planted 'pid starttime' line makes it SIGKILL any process of ours. Create the root 0700 and refuse it unless it is ours and not a symlink. (2) The owner file is written in place (336). A sweeper can read it empty between open and write, judge the live owner dead, and rmtree its directory. Write it to a temp name and rename. (3) The atexit `_remove_owner` (338) is inherited by a forked child that exits normally, which would remove the parent's live directory. Check `os.getpid()` there. (4) A failed initdb leaves pg<major>-template behind (508-527), so every later start in that process fails with 'directory not empty'. Remove it on failure. (5) An ENOTEMPTY or EACCES from `_sweep_orphans` raises into an unrelated test's setup. That is loud, so correct per the exceptions rule, but contain it per directory so one bad orphan does not fail other tests.", "files": ["packages/core/src/threetears/core/testing/services.py"], "oid": "O-6"}, {"goal": "Nothing Is Broken", "title": "the require_services backstop misses collection-time skips, and its docstring cites importorskip as covered", "recommendation": "tests/require_services.py:6 names 'an importorskip of a module the lock dropped'. A module-level `pytest.importorskip` or `pytest.skip(allow_module_level=True)` produces a skipped CollectReport, which pytest_runtest_makereport never sees. No integration file does either today. Either drop the claim from the docstring, or add a pytest_collectreport branch that fails a skipped collection under a tests/integration path while the flag is set.", "files": ["tests/require_services.py"], "oid": "O-7"}, {"goal": "Nothing Is Broken", "title": "`test-integration.sh packages/scheduled-jobs` exits 5 after a green pool run", "recommendation": "Naming a package's root as a path, when the package's only integration directory is a suite path, sends the suite dir to the pool. It also puts the root in LOCAL with `--ignore=<suite dir>`. The local pytest collects nothing and exits 5, which becomes the script's status. Skip a local path when its ignores leave nothing in it, or treat local exit 5 as 0 when every selected file went to the pool.", "files": ["scripts/test-integration.sh"], "oid": "O-8"}, {"goal": "Nothing Is Unintended", "title": "the moved public surface: RunningNats outside __all__, its lame-duck and cluster_url used only by a test, and moto absent from 3tears[testing]", "recommendation": "Consistent with the rules: the surface is `__all__`, and fixtures.py (src) calls all four exported names, so test_public_api_has_a_caller holds. RunningNats is the return type of a surface function, so leaving it out of `__all__` is defensible. Its only consumer of `enter_lame_duck` and `cluster_url` today is test_process_services.py, and W7 is planned to use them, so they are built but unconsumed until then. Process-mode S3 needs moto. The published `3tears[testing]` extra (packages/core/pyproject.toml) does not list it, and the require_services message names 'the workspace's dev dependencies', which a downstream consumer does not have. This follows D3, so no change is needed unless downstream process mode becomes a goal.", "files": ["packages/core/src/threetears/core/testing/services.py"], "oid": "O-9"}], "duration_seconds": 900, "scope": null, "scope_chosen_by": "none", "scope_unresolved_cause": "no-claim", "scope_reason": "no live plan claims `chore/integration-on-the-pool`", "base_extended_from": null, "chunks": [], "chunks_proposed": [], "chunk": null, "base_reviewed": null, "record_lint": {"records": ["docs/testing.md"], "chunk_graded": null, "chunks_graded": [], "plan_graded": null, "findings": [], "unchecked": [], "counts": {"chunk-ref-missing": null, "governed-by-gap": 0, "suite-total-claim": 0, "learnings-over-budget": 0, "learnings-budget-unreasoned": 0, "learnings-core-raise-unapproved": 0, "learnings-rule-too-long": 0, "learnings-rule-body": 0, "learnings-area-dead": 0, "change-fragment": 0, "retired-claim-survives": 0}}, "dispatched_at": "2026-11-12T06:05:46Z"}}

{"schema": 1, "kind": "review", "id": "rev-20261112T062543Z-f40b105c", "ts": "2026-11-12T06:29:12Z", "actor": {"worktree": "integ-pool", "plugin": "3.8.1-dev", "branch": "chore/integration-on-the-pool"}, "body": {"base_commit": null, "base_tree": "60a214613d1315a8ee044f55a4d47e652a68961b", "head_tree": "984abb28c8e9cbf648c2783d609ecadbe1ae9c2a", "head_commit": null, "dispatch_commit": "fc27e5d40330e57204d118217eee497a1d0260f5", "mode": "verify-resolutions (delta review, prior findings only)", "mode_chosen_by": "explicit-args", "stage": "inner", "tier": "standard", "roster": [{"role": "reviewer", "model": "claude-opus-5-5"}], "files_reviewed": [".testament.toml", "conftest.py", "docs/testing.md", "packages/core/src/threetears/core/testing/fixtures.py", "packages/core/src/threetears/core/testing/services.py", "packages/core/tests/integration/test_process_services.py", "packages/core/tests/unit/testing/test_container_stagger.py", "pyproject.toml", "scripts/test-integration.sh", "scripts/test.sh", "tests/enforcement/test_integration_suite_selection.py", "tests/enforcement/test_require_services_backstop.py", "tests/enforcement/test_secrets_marker.py", "tests/require_services.py", "tests/test_test_integration_script.py", "tests/test_test_sh_script.py", "uv.lock", "CLAUDE.md", "README.md", "packages/core/tests/integration/conftest.py", "packages/core/tests/unit/testing/test_process_services_collection.py"], "files_changed": ["CLAUDE.md", "README.md", "docs/testing.md", "packages/core/src/threetears/core/testing/services.py", "packages/core/tests/integration/conftest.py", "packages/core/tests/integration/test_process_services.py", "packages/core/tests/unit/testing/test_container_stagger.py", "packages/core/tests/unit/testing/test_process_services_collection.py", "scripts/test-integration.sh", "tests/enforcement/test_integration_suite_selection.py", "tests/enforcement/test_require_services_backstop.py", "tests/require_services.py", "tests/test_test_integration_script.py"], "files_oracle": [], "findings": [], "counts": {"blocking": 0, "warning": 0, "note": 0}, "observations": [{"goal": "Nothing Is Broken", "title": "the gate list now lives in two places: test.sh:148 and test-integration.sh:213", "recommendation": "class. The R-1 fix is right today. test-integration.sh unsets RECORD, TAVILY_API_KEY and THREETEARS_LIVE_*, which covers every name test.sh's `^(RECORD|THREETEARS_LIVE_[A-Z_]*|TAVILY_API_KEY)=` matches. But a gate added to test.sh alone brings R-1 back with no failing test, because TestEnvironmentGates hard-codes three names. ACCEPT is the default. A cheap construction to batch into a planned commit: have test.sh export the pattern it uses, or have one test assert that the two scripts' gate patterns match.", "files": ["scripts/test-integration.sh", "scripts/test.sh"], "about": {"review_id": "rev-20261112T060546Z-9c66cc62", "fid": "R-1"}, "oid": "O-1"}, {"goal": "Nothing Is Unintended", "title": "the moto socket handoff relies on werkzeug's undocumented reloader protocol (WERKZEUG_SERVER_FD); werkzeug comes in unpinned through moto", "recommendation": "instance. I checked it against the locked versions, werkzeug 3.1.9 and moto 5.2.5. moto.server calls run_simple(use_reloader=False). When WERKZEUG_RUN_MAIN=true, run_simple reads int(os.environ['WERKZEUG_SERVER_FD']) (werkzeug/serving.py:1092-1095), and pass_fds keeps the fd number in the child, so the handoff works. This is an environment protocol, not a Python private member, so the underscore rule's enforcement (tests/enforcement/_underscore_exemptions.txt) neither sees nor covers it. It is confined to one function in services.py. If a future werkzeug drops the protocol, the run fails loudly: the child still holds the inherited listener, so werkzeug's own bind gets EADDRINUSE, moto exits, and _s3_process calls pytest.fail with the log. ACCEPT. If the owner wants third-party internals recorded even when they are not underscore names, a one-line rationale beside the env construction is enough.", "files": ["packages/core/src/threetears/core/testing/services.py"], "about": {"review_id": "rev-20261112T060546Z-9c66cc62", "fid": "O-2"}, "oid": "O-2"}, {"goal": "Nothing Is Broken", "title": "the 'package in neither list runs here whole' branch lost its only test, and holds_local_tests detects integration files by text where the enforcement uses the AST", "recommendation": "instance. test_a_package_in_neither_list_runs_here_whole now pins exit 5 for a package with no integration tests, which is the right behaviour after O-8. Nothing now exercises test-integration.sh:154-157 for a package outside both lists that HAS integration tests. test_integration_suite_selection keeps that branch unreachable in the real tree. holds_local_tests (test-integration.sh:186-196) greps `mark\\.integration`, while _integration_files reads marks from the AST. Today every LOCAL_DIRS entry has a textual match: workspace has 2 of 10 files and registry 5 of 6, and the unmatched files are unit tests. ACCEPT. If either matters later, give the miniature repo a neither-list package with a marked file.", "files": ["scripts/test-integration.sh", "tests/test_test_integration_script.py"], "about": {"review_id": "rev-20261112T060546Z-9c66cc62", "fid": "O-8"}, "oid": "O-3"}], "duration_seconds": 900, "scope": null, "scope_chosen_by": "none", "scope_unresolved_cause": "no-claim", "scope_reason": "no live plan claims `chore/integration-on-the-pool`", "base_extended_from": null, "chunks": [], "chunks_proposed": [], "chunk": null, "base_reviewed": null, "record_lint": {"records": ["CLAUDE.md", "README.md", "docs/testing.md"], "chunk_graded": null, "chunks_graded": [], "plan_graded": null, "findings": [], "unchecked": [], "counts": {"chunk-ref-missing": null, "governed-by-gap": 0, "suite-total-claim": 0, "learnings-over-budget": 0, "learnings-budget-unreasoned": 0, "learnings-core-raise-unapproved": 0, "learnings-rule-too-long": 0, "learnings-rule-body": 0, "learnings-area-dead": 0, "ch